# Application code — only on the operator's word

> **EXCEPTION — PLATFORM FACTORY MODE.** When the operator has started the platform factory, this
> rule is **suspended for factory work**: the slice agents the orchestrator dispatches DO edit
> `apps/**` and `contracts_v2/**`, each inside its own slice worktree and scoped to its ticket's
> `owns` paths. See [`platform-factory-mode.mdc`](/.cursor/rules/platform-factory-mode.mdc).
> Outside factory mode this rule applies unchanged. The orchestrator itself still never edits
> these files: it dispatches a slice agent instead.

**Default: DO NOT EDIT these files in a Cursor chat.**

Application code for a ticket runs through the ticket tooling — `cargo xtask ticket run`, or
`cargo xtask platform slice-run <id>` for one ticket — with any AI coding agent, on `main` (see
[Taking a ticket from idea to shipped](/documentation_v2/runbooks/ticket_run_pipeline.md)). The
agent that writes the code updates the documentation it changes in the same commit.

## Allowed without extra permission

- Read, search, explain, review.
- Point to lines in a critique, a spec or a handoff.

## Forbidden unless the operator explicitly says "Cursor, implement this code"

- Any patch under `apps/website/api_v2/src/`, `apps/website/frontend/src/` or `apps/mod/`.
- "Fixing" audit findings yourself.
- Completing plan steps that belong to the coding agent.

## If the operator wants a fix

1. File or update the ticket and its spec and plan (mode B of
   [`cursor-agent-workflow.mdc`](/.cursor/rules/cursor-agent-workflow.mdc)); write a handoff from
   [`handoff_template.md`](/.ai/tickets/handoff_template.md) only when the context does not fit in
   the spec.
2. Tell the operator to run `cargo xtask ticket run`, or give them the prompt that
   `cargo xtask ticket prompt <id>` prints, as one fenced block.

## Documentation is not application code

Documents under `documentation_v2/`, README.md files and the ticket files are edited in mode B
without this permission. When the operator does authorize code in the chat, that code's
documentation changes land in the same commit as the code.
